  return (-T15 - np.uint32(S1(e8)) - Ch(np.uint32(e8), e7, e6))
  return (-T15 - np.uint32(S1(e8)) - Ch(np.uint32(e8), e7, e6))
Which ABOVE-DIAGONAL dependencies can context choice clear?
C_j absorbs a_{j+1} (the diagonal, always present and wanted).
C0's row is special: its dependence on a2,a3,.. is frozen provisionally
and paid for by the consistency residual, which the family collapses.
For an extra round to be free, C3 must absorb a4, which needs
C1 free of BOTH a3 and a4, and C2 free of a4.

context conditions                  C1 free of a3  C1 free of a4  C2 free of a4   verdict
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
random context                              False          False          False   nothing cleared
family a4=a5, e8=e9=-1                       True          False          False   iteration removed only
family + a6=a5                               True          False          False   iteration removed only
shifted a5=a6, e9=e10=-1                    False          False           True   nothing cleared
TRIPLE a4=a5=a6, e8=e9=e10=-1                True          False           True   iteration removed only
QUAD a4..a7 equal, e8..e11=-1                True          False           True   iteration removed only

Also: does the consistency residual still collapse under each?
